.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt IW 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm iw
.Nd show and configure wireless devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl debug
.Ar command
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl debug
.Cm dev Ar ifname
.Ar command
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl debug
.Cm phy Ar phyname
.Ar command
.Nm
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is Linux's configuration program for wireless devices, version 6.17.
It speaks to the kernel's nl80211 interface, in which each radio is a
.Em phy ,
such as
.Cm phy0 ,
and each of its network interfaces, such as
.Cm wlan0 ,
has a type: a station, an access point, a monitor or a mesh point.
A command for an interface follows
.Cm dev Ar ifname ,
and one for a radio follows
.Cm phy Ar phyname ;
either word may be left out where the name is unambiguous.
.Pp
The commands used most are these:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm dev
List the interfaces of each radio, with their address, type and channel.
.It Cm phy , list
List each radio's bands, channels, rates, ciphers, interface types and
commands.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm info
The interface's radio, address, type and channel.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm scan Op Cm ssid Ar name ...
Scan and list the access points found, with their frequency, signal,
security and name; given names, look for those directly.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm scan dump
List the results of the last scan without scanning again.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm link
The access point a station is joined to, with the signal and rates.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm station dump
The stations the interface knows: the access point of a station, or the
clients of an access point.
A station's
.Sy tx bitrate
is the rate of its last data frame the access point acknowledged, and its
.Sy rx bitrate
that of the last frame it received from the access point.
Its
.Sy rx drop misc
counts the frames it received and dropped, replays and duplicates among
them.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm connect Ar ssid Op Ar freq
Join an open network.
A secured network is joined with
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 .
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm disconnect
Leave the network.
.It Cm reg get , reg set Ar CC
Show the regulatory domain, or set it to that of country
.Ar CC .
.It Cm phy Ar phyname Cm interface add Ar ifname Cm type Ar type
Add an interface of
.Ar type
.Pq Cm managed , ap , monitor , mesh
to the radio.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm del
Remove the interface.
.It Cm dev Ar ifname Cm set power_save on|off
Let the station sleep between beacons, or keep it awake.
.It Cm help Op Ar command
List the commands, or those that begin with
.Ar command .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl debug
Print the netlink messages exchanged with the kernel.
.It Fl Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find the radio, scan, and see the link once wpa_supplicant has joined:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
iw dev
iw dev wlan0 scan
iw dev wlan0 link
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hostapd 8 ,
.Xr rfkill 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
